          "id": 490911240,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I know, the spec states:\nhttps://github.com/rfbproto/rfbproto/blob/master/rfbproto.rst#vencrypt\n\nAfter that server sends one byte response which indicates if everything is OK. Non-zero value means failure and connection will be closed. Zero value means success.\n\nThere's no explanation on different non-zero error codes. So any non-zero byte value should lead to \"Error\", right?",
